From a59f66c17705488dbaa1ff143279ff6606b18eb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:56:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] [clang][Driver] Support the AArch64 GNU ILP32 ABI on
 Linux

Make clang usable as the compiler driver for aarch64[_be]-linux-gnu_ilp32,
following GCC's aarch64-linux-gnu toolchains:

- -mabi=ilp32 selects the gnu_ilp32 environment for AArch64 GNU/Linux
  targets and -mabi=lp64 selects gnu again; both use the AAPCS64 procedure
  call standard ("-target-abi aapcs").
- The dynamic linker is /lib/ld-linux-aarch64[_be]_ilp32.so.1 and the GNU
  ld emulation is aarch64linux32[b].
- Libraries live in libilp32 (GCC's multilib OS directory for ILP32), and
  the multiarch triple is aarch64[_be]-linux-gnu_ilp32.

Signed-off-by: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
